From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:38:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] adb: record the USB debugging setting in
 persist.sys.usb.config

AdbService reads persist.sys.usb.config at every boot and rewrites the
adb_enabled setting from it, and UsbDeviceManager is what writes the
property when the setting changes. This product has no UsbDeviceManager
(it needs /sys/class/android_usb), so nothing recorded the setting:
USB debugging was off again after every reboot.

The handler of every change of adb_enabled now writes the property:
"adb" when USB debugging is on, empty when it is off, the values the
stock manager writes. The property, the setting and adbd agree within
the observer's hop, and adbd reads the property to decide whether a key
other than the host's may authenticate.
---
 services/core/java/com/android/server/adb/AdbService.java | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/adb/AdbService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/adb/AdbService.java
index 2f819bfaf5e7da332160c870900a12be3993a6e7..b03c920bffd4ff2ec36a9bf2ffa2ebdcf8865e7f 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/adb/AdbService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/adb/AdbService.java
@@ -448,6 +448,12 @@ public class AdbService extends IAdbManager.Stub {
                     return;
                 }
                 mIsAdbUsbEnabled = enable;
+                // This product has no UsbDeviceManager, the property's other writer, so record the
+                // setting here: systemReady() reads it back at the next boot, and adbd reads it to
+                // decide whether a key other than the host's may authenticate.
+                Slog.d(TAG, "kernarium: USB debugging is now " + enable);
+                SystemProperties.set(
+                        USB_PERSISTENT_CONFIG_PROPERTY, enable ? UsbManager.USB_FUNCTION_ADB : "");
                 break;
             case AdbTransportType.WIFI:
                 if (enable == mIsAdbWifiEnabled) {
